      "question_html": "Solve: \\( 3x^{2/3} - 5 = 22 \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q3_x",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "x =",
          "answer": 27,
          "tolerance": 0.01
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Add 5, then divide by 3 to isolate x^(2/3). Then raise to 3/2.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "3x^(2/3) = 27 → x^(2/3) = 9.",
        "Raise to 3/2: x = 9^(3/2).",
        "9^(1/2) = 3, then 3³ = 27.",
        "Check: 3(27)^(2/3) - 5 = 3·9 - 5 = 27 - 5 = 22 ✓"
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Two-step isolation, then 9^(3/2) = 27.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Isolate x^(2/3) completely before raising to the 3/2 power."
    },
